NOTE ON THE ENDPOINT CHOICE (faithfulness)
------------------------------------------
The @astrojs/node adapter additionally ships its own `node` image endpoint whose PRODUCTION local
branch has an unrelated dist/-assets path check (`filePath.startsWith(assetsDir)`) that returns 500
before the remote fallback, incidentally shadowing this SSRF in a node standalone build. The CVE
actually affects the `generic` endpoint — the endpoint every SSR/serverless deployment uses and the one
Astro's dev server exercises for the node endpoint's DEV branch. It is selected here via the PUBLIC
`image.endpoint.entrypoint` config option. The guard under test (isRemotePath in
@astrojs/internal-helpers) is byte-identical between the two endpoints, so the version differential is
exactly the CVE chain. This was determined empirically by reading the real installed endpoint sources
and testing the node endpoint (500, no sidecar fetch) vs the generic endpoint (flag returned).

